; ====================================================================
; TDD 03: OP_MXV Payload Decoding and Semiring Stub
;
; Tests that OP_MXV strictly obeys the 8-bit src_vec, 8-bit rel,
; 16-bit semiring_id bitshift layout in the bytecode payload.
; ====================================================================
; {EXPECT: STATUS = IMPULSE_VM_OK}

.text
; We won't run a full MXV because it requires graph topology.
; Instead we will use invalid register offsets that should trap.
; R1000 is invalid.
; C++ expects: src=255, rel=255, semiring=0
; Payload = (0 << 16) | (255 << 8) | 255 = 0x00FFFF = 65535
; If Java reads this as src = 65535 & 0xFFFF = 65535, it will hit register 65535 instead of 255.

; We use an assertion or just let it fail.
; Actually, since the op is stubbed/broken, the test is simply that the VM 
; correctly parses the arguments without corrupting the register indices.
0x00: OP_INIT_INPUT_SET R1, 0
0x01: OP_MXV R2, R1, 1, 0
0x02: OP_HALT
